      "author_association": "NONE",
      "body": "The following code, when switching between lines 14 and 15 (the two versions of the `for` line), oscillates between compiling and not compiling because it requires `Sync` for the `dyn Send` items:\r\n```rust\r\n#![feature(async_await, await_macro, futures_api)]\r\n\r\nuse std::collections::VecDeque;\r\nuse std::future::Future;\r\n\r\npub async fn receive<HandleFn, Fut, Ret>(handle: HandleFn) -> Ret\r\nwhere\r\n    Fut: Future<Output = ()>,\r\n    HandleFn: Fn() -> Fut,\r\n{\r\n    let v: VecDeque<Box<dyn Send>> = VecDeque::new();\r\n\r\n    let l = v.len();\r\n    for _i in 0..v.len() {\r\n    //for _i in 0..l {\r\n        await!(handle());\r\n    }\r\n    \r\n    loop {}\r\n}\r\n\r\nfn do_stuff<F: Future + Send>(_f: F) {}\r\n\r\npub fn showcase() {\r\n    do_stuff(async {\r\n        match await!(receive(async move || ())) {\r\n            true => \"test\",\r\n            false => \"test\",\r\n        };\r\n    });\r\n}\r\n```\r\n[(playground)](https://play.rust-lang.org/?version=nightly&mode=debug&edition=2018&gist=9110c0064a66d987a9eff38ab282c8c0)\r\n\r\n(Note: this is a simplification of the failure that occurs on https://github.com/Ekleog/erlust/commit/98c6cbc88805b11833b9129c457b38d68a7be970 when running `cargo test`)",
